---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Karl Kugler’s explorations across software, robotics, electronics, and artificial life."
>
  <header class="page-intro container">
    <span class="eyebrow">A LITTLE CONTEXT</span>
    <h1>
      Hi, I’m Karl<span class="accent">.</span>
      <br />
      <em>I like figuring things out.</em>
    </h1>
  </header>
  <section class="container page-body">
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-monogram" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>k.</span>
        <span class="eyebrow">A WORKBENCH, NOT A FINISH LINE.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="about-copy">
        <h2>
          Somewhere between
          <br />
          code and the real world.
        </h2>
        <p>
          This is a home for my projects and the questions that run through
          them: how to make physical measurements inspectable, how simple rules
          shape a simulated world, and how to build useful software around both.
        </p>
        <p>
          The work crosses software, electronics, robotics, and AI. I’m
          interested in the details that make a system understandable — clear
          boundaries, visible state, and honest explanations of what a result
          can and cannot show.
        </p>
        <p>
          Here you’ll find a tactile hand viewer, an artificial-life laboratory,
          and technical notes that follow the work. Each project has its own
          story; the common thread is learning by making.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link mt-6" href="/projects/">
          Take a look at the work <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="capabilities">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">01 / PHYSICAL SYSTEMS</span>
        <h3>Make it observable.</h3>
        <p>
          Robotic hand telemetry, tactile data, articulated visualization, and
          the boundary between a measurement and its interpretation.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">02 / SOFTWARE</span>
        <h3>Make it understandable.</h3>
        <p>
          Python, JavaScript, C++, and browser interfaces. Modular tools that
          connect data, behavior, and a useful view of the system.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">03 / EXPERIMENTS</span>
        <h3>Keep asking.</h3>
        <p>
          Artificial life, inherited neural controllers, and controlled
          comparisons. Interesting behavior is a starting point for
          investigation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
